{
  "manufacturer": "Laars",
  "manufacturer_slug": "laars",
  "model": "Sola control - ProtoNode",
  "model_slug": "sola-protonode",
  "aliases": [
    "Sola",
    "Laars Sola",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N34",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N35",
    "FPC-N34-0701",
    "Laars ProtoNode"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller gateway",
  "applies_to": "Laars boilers with the Sola control, read through a ProtoNode FPC-N34 gateway (the document does not name the models).",
  "summary": "The ProtoNode reads the Sola control over Modbus RTU and serves 88 objects per boiler: 64 analog inputs and 24 analog values. The AIs cover sensors, firing rate, burner and CH/DHW status codes, pump status and lead-lag slave states; the AVs hold CH enable, CH, DHW and lead-lag setpoints, time-of-day setpoints and resettable counters.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50000 + device Node-ID",
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Each boiler on the ProtoNode's RS-485 bus shows up as its own BACnet device, and every one uses the same object IDs. The device instance is Node_Offset (default 50000) plus the boiler's Node-ID, so Node-ID 1 = device 50001.",
    "The mapping has no read/write column. AV, BV and MV objects are mapped to Metasys N2 outputs and LonWorks input variables, so they are listed here as writable; AI, BI and MI objects are read-only.",
    "No units or state texts are given. The LonWorks SNVT types in the source show which values are temperatures and which are hours.",
    "Runtime and cycle counters that span two Modbus registers (e.g. 40131/40132) are one object each.",
    "Weil-McLain publishes its own ProtoNode list for Sola boilers with different object numbers; use the list from the boiler's maker."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Write CH Enable and the CH setpoint (or the lead-lag setpoint on a lead-lag master), then read back CH status, the burner sequence, outlet temperature, firing rate and the lockout code. The mapping gives no values or units, so check written values against the boiler display.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 76",
        "name": "CH Enable",
        "why": "Central heat enable"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 46",
        "name": "CH setpoint",
        "why": "Central heat water setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 50",
        "name": "Lead Lag setpoint",
        "why": "Setpoint for a lead-lag (cascade) master"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 19",
        "name": "CH status",
        "why": "Central heat status code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 71",
        "name": "Burner Control Sequence",
        "why": "Burner sequence state"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Outlet sensor",
        "why": "Outlet water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "Firing rate",
        "why": "Burner firing rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 16",
        "name": "Lockout code",
        "why": "Lockout status code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "AV 76 CH Enable is the writable enable. The mapping does not give its values or say how it interacts with the boiler's own enable settings. AV 87 Burner Switch is also writable but is not explained.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device instance = Node_Offset + boiler Node-ID. Node_Offset defaults to 50000 and is changed in the ProtoNode web configurator; Node-IDs must be unique, 1-255.",
      "Boiler to ProtoNode: Modbus RTU, 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
      "Default ProtoNode IP address 192.168.1.24, mask 255.255.255.0. Choose BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP with the Protocol Selector, then add one profile per device with its Node-ID.",
      "With more than one device on a ProtoNode, set BACnet Virtual Server Nodes to Yes. For BACnet MS/TP also set MAC address, baud rate and Max Master.",
      "Two or more ProtoNodes on the same subnet need different BACnet Network Numbers (default 50).",
      "A ProtoNode handles 1,500 registers in total; this profile uses 88 per device."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "No units or state texts are given; CH status, burner sequence and lockout codes must be decoded with the Sola documentation.",
      "AV 85/86 Password Reg 1/2 are writable but not explained in the mapping.",
      "Counters (burner run time, pump and burner cycle counts) are AVs, so the BMS can overwrite them."
    ]
  },
